# ─── VOX server (server/) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to server/.env locally, or /opt/vox/.env on the VPS, and fill in.
# NEVER commit the real file.
#
#   cp server/.env.example server/.env
#
# server/deploy.sh generates MASTER_KEY and BOOTSTRAP_SECRET automatically on
# a first deploy if /opt/vox/.env is absent, and prints the bootstrap secret
# once. You only need to write this file by hand for local development.
#
# Legend:  [required]  the server refuses to start without it
#          [optional]  feature is disabled or falls back if unset

# ─── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [optional] development | test | production        (default: development)
NODE_ENV=production
# [optional] Port for the HTTP server. Binds to 127.0.0.1 only; Nginx
#            terminates TLS and proxies to it.                (default: 3000)
PORT=3000
# [optional] SQLite file. Created with its parent directory on first boot.
#                                                   (default: ./data/vox.db)
DB_PATH=/opt/vox/data/vox.db
# [optional] fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace          (default: info)
LOG_LEVEL=info

# ─── Security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] 32 random bytes, base64. Encrypts every third-party credential
#            at rest (AES-256-GCM). Losing it makes stored credentials
#            unrecoverable — they must be re-entered. Rotating it requires
#            re-entering them too.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
MASTER_KEY=your_base64_32_byte_key_here

# [optional but needed once] Seeds the first user on an empty database. The
#            server stores only an Argon2id hash of it. This is the value the
#            glasses and dashboard authenticate with. Rotate it from the
#            dashboard after pairing.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=your_shared_secret_here

# ─── URLs and domains ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] Public origin of THIS server. Twilio signs webhooks against the
#            full URL it called, so a mismatch here makes every inbound SMS
#            fail signature verification with a 403.
TWILIO_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=https://your-server-domain.example
# [optional] Public origin used for outbound attribution headers, e.g.
#            OpenRouter's HTTP-Referer.   (default: TWILIO_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL)
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-server-domain.example

# ─── Twilio (SMS) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [optional here] Preferred path is the dashboard setup wizard, which stores
#            these encrypted in the database. These env vars are the
#            bootstrap fallback; the database wins when both are present.
#            Without Twilio, SMS is unavailable — email still works.
# TWILIO_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_TOKEN=your_twilio_auth_token_here
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+15555550100
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=MGxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Speech to text ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required for voice] OpenAI key, used for Whisper transcription. This is
#            the same key as the OpenAI LLM provider below — set it once.
#            Without it the glasses can record but not transcribe.
# OPENAI_KEY=sk-your_openai_key_here

# ─── AI / LLM (at least one required for compose) ────────────────────────
# Used for intent parsing and the seven tone rewrites. Pick a provider in
# the dashboard; that choice decides which key is read.
# ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-your_anthropic_key_here
# OPENROUTER_KEY=sk-or-your_openrouter_key_here
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_KEY=your_ollama_cloud_key_here
# [optional] Override base URLs — rarely needed.
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1

# ─── Email ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Email is NOT configured here. SMTP and IMAP credentials are entered in the
# dashboard (Integrations → Email account) and stored encrypted in the
# database with MASTER_KEY, because they are per-user rather than per-server.
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
